    <p class="security-versus">
        <strong>Versus Discord:</strong> Discord has done serious work encrypting calls, and we respect that. But your text messages,
        which is most of what people write, remain readable by Discord, and everything runs on its servers. Our difference is that
        private text, not just calls, is protected, that nothing is stored centrally, and that communities can run on infrastructure
        they control.
    </p>
    <p class="security-versus">
        <strong>Versus Signal:</strong> Signal sets the standard for private messaging, and we build on the same ideas. Where we
        differ is purpose. Signal is for private conversations. We bring the same protections to public communities, community
        servers and a desktop-first experience built for gamers.
    </p>

    <h2>What we don't protect against</h2>
    <p>No system is perfect, and you should know where the limits are.</p>
    <ul class="security-limits">
        <li><strong>A compromised device.</strong> If someone controls your computer or phone, encryption can't help. Keep your system updated.</li>
        <li><strong>Metadata.</strong> To deliver a message, a relay has to know where it is going and when. We minimise what we collect and keep. <mark>[Describe what is logged and for how long.]</mark></li>
        <li><strong>People in the conversation.</strong> End-to-end encryption keeps outsiders out. It can't stop someone you've chatted with from screenshotting or sharing what you said. In large public channels, anyone who joins can read them.</li>
        <li><strong>Servers you don't run.</strong> If you join someone else's community server, the operator can see who connects to it. Choose communities you trust.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Verifying our claims</h2>
    <p>
        Security claims should be checkable, so we aim to make ours so.
        <mark>[Choose what is true for your project: publish the source code, publish the protocol design, commission an independent review, run a vulnerability disclosure process with a contact address.]</mark>
        We will publish the results of any review, including the problems found.
    </p>

    <div class="security-summary">
        <p><strong>Summary:</strong> We protect your messages by design: encrypted on your device, relayed without being stored, kept only where you keep them, and hosted by communities that you choose. That is the security model.</p>
    </div>

</div>
